# Written BEFORE `git init`, which is the only time it is free.
# A .gitignore added after the first commit does not un-commit anything --
# secrets stay in history until the history is rewritten. This repo is not yet
# a git repo, so everything below has never been tracked and never will be.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# 🚨 SECRETS -- the reason this file exists
# .env currently holds ELEVEN live credentials: UW_API_KEY, WEBULL_APP_KEY,
# WEBULL_APP_SECRET, WEBULL_ACCOUNT_ID, MAIN_WALLET, AGENT_SECRET,
# RITHMIC_USER, RITHMIC_PWD, DB_KEY, TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN, TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID.
# conf/token.txt holds a live Webull access token, rewritten on every start.
# Publishing this toolkit is a stated goal; `git add .` without this file
# would push a funded trading account's keys to a public remote.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
conf/
*.pem
*.key

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# EXECUTION LEDGERS -- real (paper) trading activity, and the amended copies.
# Observational records, not code. They are also the files reconcile/rebuild
# scripts rewrite, so they would churn every session.
*.jsonl
*.jsonl.bak-*
# Extension-independent: bot_executions_log.txt holds the SAME JSONL ledger
# with a different suffix, so the *.jsonl rule sails straight past it. Match on
# the name, not the extension -- a leak rule keyed to a file extension only
# holds until someone saves a copy.
bot_executions*
flow_trigger*
gex_history*
manual_executions*
hl_executions*
gamma_hedge_executions*

# 🚨 AND THE POINT ABOVE PROVED ITSELF. Audited 2026-09-26: the rule
# `*.jsonl.bak-*` required a HYPHEN after "bak", so it covered
#   manual_executions.jsonl.bak-20260923-130019     (ignored)
# and missed
#   manual_executions.jsonl.bak2-130057             (would have been COMMITTED)
#   manual_executions.jsonl.bak3-130710             (would have been COMMITTED)
# -- four files of real fills, entry and exit prices and P&L, created by hand
# during the 2026-09-23 ledger repair when "bak" had already been used. Also
# missed: manual_orders.py.mojibake.bak, 45 KB of the corrupted source kept as
# a recovery copy. One glob, matching any suffix after .bak:
*.bak*
*.mojibake*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# DATA -- regenerable from the API, and far too large for a repo.
# lake/ alone runs to gigabytes per session of full tape.
lake/
historical/
*.parquet
*.csv
_*_cache/

# Viewer tape: regenerated by `python export_flow_tape.py`, ~50 MB of session
# JSON derived entirely from lake/ + historical/, both already ignored above.
# flow_viewer.html itself is source and IS tracked.
tape/
# 🚨 BOTH EXTENSIONS. `export_flow_tape.py` writes _trade_tape.json AND
# _trade_tape.js (the same payload wrapped for a <script> tag, so the viewer can
# be opened from file:// without a server). Only the .json was listed, so the
# 1.2 MB .js was the single largest file in the would-be commit -- larger than
# bot_runner.py -- and it is pure derived output. Third time this repo has been
# caught by an ignore rule keyed to an extension.
_trade_tape.*
_*.json
# live/state.json is bot_runner's own state, written every 5s during RTH --
# ephemeral, and it names open positions.
live/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# LOGS AND SCRATCH
*.log
daily_log.txt
webull_data*.log
# 🚨 ROTATED LOGS DO NOT END IN .log. The Webull SDK rotates to
# `webull_data_sdk.log.2026-09-24_11`, where the extension is no longer last, so
# BOTH `*.log` and `webull_data*.log` sail past it -- eight such files were
# sitting untracked-but-unignored on 2026-09-26. They carry no credentials (the
# SDK logs the token file's PATH, not its contents), but they do print
# `C:\Users\<name>\Desktop\Cleanbot\conf\token.txt` and the server's
# `/root/bot_engine/...`, which is free reconnaissance and a real name.
*.log.*

# Research scratch output. ~31 files at the repo root, all regenerable by
# re-running the check_*.py that wrote them, none of it source.
# 🚨 INCLUDING _install_key.txt, which is the authorized_keys one-liner for the
# cloud box: a PUBLIC key, so not a credential, but it names the laptop's
# hostname and spells out the exact install path for the trading server's root
# login. `_*.json` covered _viewer.json; nothing covered the .txt beside it.
_*.txt

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# THIRD-PARTY MATERIAL -- not ours to republish. See NOTICE.
#
# 🚨 A PORT IS A DERIVATIVE WORK, NOT AN INDEPENDENT ONE.
# smartmoneyalgo.txt is a TradingView Pine script, "© QuantAlgo", carrying an
# explicit CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 header. smart_money_flow.py is a self-declared
# "faithful port" of it and check_smart_money_flow.py is that port's test -- so
# BOTH inherit the original's NonCommercial and ShareAlike terms, which conflict
# with the Apache 2.0 licence on the rest of this repo. Shipping the .py while
# excluding the .txt would have been the worst of the options: the derivative
# published, the licence it derives from nowhere in sight.
# The research finding stands in METHODOLOGY.md; the code stays local.
smartmoneyalgo.txt
smart_money_flow.py
check_smart_money_flow.py

# Rithmic's protobuf schema, distributed by Rithmic to its own API customers
# under their agreement. rithmic_streamer.py ships and expects you to regenerate
# these from the schema Rithmic gives you; nothing in the directional bot uses
# this path at all.
rithmic_protos/

# Local editor workspace: Cleanbot.code-workspace lists sibling folders from
# this machine (../vita, ../../Downloads/...), which is someone else's project
# names and a map of a private disk.
*.code-workspace

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# PYTHON
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# EDITOR / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
